      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sterling Ranch was founded by the Sterling family in the 1860s and stayed ranching for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sterlingranchcab.com/399/Our-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1980 Frank and Joy Burns bought the original 2,200‑acre ranch from a Denver bank, sparking its modern transformation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sterlingranchcab.com/399/Our-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Smethills acquired the ranch in 2004, added neighboring parcels, and envisioned a 3,500‑acre eco‑conscious community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sterlingranchcab.com/399/Our-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Construction of the master‑planned community began in 2016, with eight builders offering single‑family homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sterling_Ranch%2C_Colorado"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sterling Ranch will eventually host 12,050 homes and 33,000 residents across 3,500 acres, including 30 miles of trails and open space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sterlingranchcab.com/399/Our-History"
    },
    {
